1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,160
每天下午我都去盧克的學校
Every afternoon, I've been going to Luke's campus

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:03,880
幫他為橄欖球選拔賽做訓練
to help him train for rugby tryouts.

3
00:00:04,831 --> 00:00:07,262
我們再練最后一遍舉人爭球怎么樣
What do you say we practice that lineout lift one last time?

4
00:00:07,262 --> 00:00:08,627
-來... -我得走了
- And... - I got to go.

5
00:00:08,627 --> 00:00:10,232
我可不想耽誤了女性研究課[時間]
I don't want to be late for women's studies.

6
00:00:10,232 --> 00:00:11,697
我都是這么叫我的午休時間
That's what I call my lunch break.

7
00:00:11,816 --> 00:00:12,864
好吧
All right.

8
00:00:13,152 --> 00:00:14,636
祝你選拔會好運
Good luck at tryouts.

9
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:16,003
前幾天
The other day,

10
00:00:16,052 --> 00:00:19,749
有個很有意思的東西吸引了我的目光
something pretty interesting caught my eye.

11
00:00:21,582 --> 00:00:23,486
為了使微觀經濟過程
modifications must be made

12
00:00:23,486 --> 00:00:26,425
與供求分析相符
to standard microeconomic procedures

13
00:00:26,425 --> 00:00:30,202
需要做出一些修正
to apply supply and demand analysis.

14
00:00:30,621 --> 00:00:33,760
首先 我們構建一個效用函數
First, we construct a utility function,

15
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,773
這里Y軸表示收入
where Y equals income

16
00:00:35,773 --> 00:00:38,274
X軸表示服務的成本
and X equals the cost of services.

17
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:39,700
這個嘛
Well...

18
00:00:40,327 --> 00:00:43,586
接下來 我們要么改變X
Uh, next, we vary either X --

19
00:00:44,732 --> 00:00:46,216
什么 你有什么高見
What -- What's on your mind?

20
00:00:46,246 --> 00:00:49,366
恕我直言
Well, um, with all due respect,

21
00:00:49,605 --> 00:00:51,867
這有滿滿一房間有抱負的房地產經紀人
uh, you have a roomful of aspiring Realtors here,

22
00:00:51,867 --> 00:00:54,229
我擔心你可能用這堆數字公式
and I worry that you might be turning them off

23
00:00:54,229 --> 00:00:57,079
毀了他們的興趣
with all those numbers and formulas.

24
00:00:57,158 --> 00:00:59,331
這可是一項激動人心的事業
It's actually a very exciting business.

25
00:00:59,331 --> 00:01:02,231
是一項跟人與情感
It's about people and -- and emotional connections

26
00:01:02,231 --> 00:01:04,144
還有印了你肖像的磁鐵息息相關的事業
and magnets with your face on them.

27
00:01:04,144 --> 00:01:06,167
你覺得你能大搖大擺走進來
You think you can just walk in here

28
00:01:06,167 --> 00:01:07,981
然后開始教課嗎
and start teaching this class?

29
00:01:07,981 --> 00:01:09,226
對不起 我不應該
I'm so sorry. I shouldn't have --

30
00:01:09,226 --> 00:01:11,349
不 我是在問你 你能替我教這個嗎
No, I'm asking -- can you teach this class for me?

31
00:01:11,349 --> 00:01:14,199
要是我現在走 停車費會劃算許多
If I leave now, I won't have to pay the all-day parking rate.

32
00:01:17,866 --> 00:01:18,992
跟院長談了十分鐘
10 minutes with the dean,

33
00:01:18,992 --> 00:01:21,384
結果發現 我曾賣給他一間房
who, it turns out, I'd sold a house to,

34
00:01:21,384 --> 00:01:22,729
現在我正式入職了
and I was official.

35
00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:25,020
想象一下菲爾·鄧菲
Imagine Phil Dunphy shaping minds

36
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:27,580
在神圣的紅衫社區大學
in the hallowed halls of Sequoia Community College,

37
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:29,440
這建校長達兩年的大學教書
established 2016.

38
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:32,300
大家能看到這個表格
As you can see from this graph,

39
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:35,860
不是關于X和Y的
it's not about X's and Y's.

40
00:01:36,442 --> 00:01:40,129
而是關于嘿和哈的
It's about oohs and ahs.

41
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:44,440
好
Mm. Okay.

42
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:46,600
那么 房地產等于什么呢
So, what does real estate equal?

43
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:52,200
眼神交流
eye contact.

44
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:09,480
好了 你的早餐快準備好了
All right. Your breakfast is almost ready.

45
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:11,880
你今天庭審需要多吃點攢足力氣
You're gonna need all your energy for the courtroom today

46
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,240
以防你得放聲呼號"是我不守規矩嗎
in case you have to yell, "I'm out of order?

47
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:14,180
是你無視規則
You're out of order.

48
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:15,980
是這該死的體制一塌糊涂"
The whole damn system's out of order!"

49
00:02:16,004 --> 00:02:16,851
估計不會
Might not do that.

50
00:02:16,851 --> 00:02:19,023
我覺得會贏 所以現在是這體制的鐵粉
I think I'm winning, so big fan of the system right now.

51
00:02:19,023 --> 00:02:19,980
-反正讓我這個前輩 -小卡
- Anyway, it can't hurt - Cam.

52
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:23,160
看一眼這個案子又沒什么壞處
to have some experienced eyes take a look at this police work.

53
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:24,980
馬馬虎虎 無聊 沒意思
Sloppy. Sloppy, sloppy.

54
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:27,920
行了 我知道你自命什么名偵探
Okay, I know you fancy yourself some sort of detective.

55
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:30,740
你知道嗎 我小時候就是個業余小偵探呢
You know, I was quite the amateur sleuth as a boy,

56
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,460
現實生活中的百科全書
a real-life Encyclopedia Brown.

57
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,700
大家都叫我知識索引瓊斯
They called me Thesaurus Jones.

58
00:02:33,742 --> 00:02:35,855
我現在真的需要安靜一會兒
What I really need right now is just a few minutes of silence,

59
00:02:35,855 --> 00:02:37,469
比如 要我說最難的案子
just like -- I would say my toughest case

60
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:40,020
那得是"消失的雪人之謎"
was "The Case of the Missing Snowman."

61
00:02:40,289 --> 00:02:42,541
一開始 我以為他活過來了
You know, at first, I thought he'd come to life,

62
00:02:42,541 --> 00:02:43,976
-結果 -噓 在講我的庭審
- but turns out - Oh. Shh! My trial!

63
00:02:43,976 --> 00:02:46,916
今天是地檢進行證人問詢的第四天
Today marks the fourth day of witness questioning by the DA's office.

64
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:47,740
我的天啊
Oh, my God.

65
00:02:47,973 --> 00:02:48,839
那是你嗎
Is that you?

66
00:02:48,839 --> 00:02:50,344
我看上去像一個小精靈剛剛走進了
I look like an elf that just walked

67
00:02:50,344 --> 00:02:51,191
自己的驚喜派對
into his own surprise party.

68
00:02:51,191 --> 00:02:53,194
不 像我們倆那次用微波爐熱的南瓜
No, it's like the time we tried to microwave a squash.

69
00:02:53,194 --> 00:02:55,596
我 這可是我的第一次大型庭審
I -- Okay, this is my first big trial,

70
00:02:55,596 --> 00:02:57,639
一個 一個讓我名聲大噪的機會
a-a chance to make a name for myself.

71
00:02:57,900 --> 00:03:00,580
現在所有人會討論的都是這張丑畫了
All anyone's gonna be talking about is that awful picture!

72
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:01,980
這簡直是場災難
Okay, this is a disaster.

73
00:03:01,994 --> 00:03:03,269
市中心有個地方
Th-- There's a place downtown

74
00:03:03,269 --> 00:03:04,475
所有的律師都在那喝酒
where all the lawyers go to drink.

75
00:03:04,475 --> 00:03:05,701
叫旁廳酒吧
It's called The Side Bar.

76
00:03:05,701 --> 00:03:07,734
他們把每一個人首次大型庭審的
They put courtroom sketches on the wall

77
00:03:07,734 --> 00:03:09,159
素描畫掛在墻上
of everyone's first big trial.

78
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,600
可能沒人看到呢
Maybe nobody saw it.

79
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:15,360
未必是壞事 說不定只是安珀警報呢
Don't assume the worst. It could just be an Amber Alert.

80
00:03:17,878 --> 00:03:18,965
-老爸好 -在呢
- Hey, Dad. - Yo.

81
00:03:18,965 --> 00:03:20,519
既然這是我們第一天和新的合作伙伴見面
Since it's our first day with our new partners,

82
00:03:20,519 --> 00:03:21,605
我覺得你這次上班是不是
I thought maybe you could get to work

83
00:03:21,605 --> 00:03:24,157
能盡量準時
as close to on time as poss--

84
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,860
我盡量
I will try my best.

85
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:28,520
大家好
Hi.

86
00:03:29,109 --> 00:03:30,365
不好意思 我遲到了嗎
I'm sorry. Am I late?

87
00:03:30,365 --> 00:03:31,172
沒有 沒有 沒 沒
No, no, no, no. Oh.

88
00:03:31,172 --> 00:03:32,846
我們對時間要求沒那么嚴格
And we're not real time sticklers here. Ah.

89
00:03:32,846 --> 00:03:34,441
我們發現員工按照自己的節奏工作
We've found that team members really excel

90
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:36,240
能事半功倍
when they follow their own energy rhythms.

91
00:03:36,314 --> 00:03:37,361
有點意思 因為我發現
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Interesting, 'cause I've found

92
00:03:37,361 --> 00:03:38,526
員工們在公司還沒倒閉之前
team members are happiest

93
00:03:38,526 --> 00:03:40,300
才是最高興的
when the company stays in business,

94
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:43,091
也就是說9點前到崗
which means asses in chairs by 9:00.

95
00:03:44,266 --> 00:03:46,608
爸 你能跟我出來一小會嗎
Dad, could I just have a quick -- quick sec with you?

96
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:47,340
行啊
Sure.

97
00:03:49,169 --> 00:03:50,305
是這樣的 爸 你看
Um...so, Dad, look,

98
00:03:50,305 --> 00:03:52,647
這里的公司文化不一樣
the culture is just different here.

99
00:03:52,647 --> 00:03:54,820
你不能帶著打壓的態度進去
And you just can't come in with a sledgehammer,

100
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:56,215
不然氣氛會很緊張
or it's gonna create tension.

101
00:03:56,215 --> 00:03:57,849
你不想讓他們疏遠你吧
You don't want to alienate people.

102
00:03:57,849 --> 00:03:59,862
-所以你想讓我改變真我 -不是
- So you want me to change who I am? - No.

103
00:03:59,862 --> 00:04:02,642
我想讓你先把真我收起來
I just want you to hide who you are.

104
00:04:02,642 --> 00:04:04,048
我是說 來 就改變一點
I mean, come on. Just a little bit.

105
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,500
把這個摘了
Let's get rid of this.

106
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:07,260
看看 這就好多了
Look at that. That's better already.

107
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,740
這個50出頭的帥大叔是誰呀
Who is this 50-something, huh?

108
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:12,200
-行吧 我努力好好表現 -謝謝 老爸
-Fine. I will be on my best behavior. -Thanks, Dad.

109
00:04:12,857 --> 00:04:15,239
剛剛真不好意思
So sorry about that.

110
00:04:15,239 --> 00:04:16,116
沒關系
Well, it's no problem.

111
00:04:16,116 --> 00:04:17,650
-和家人的時光很重要嘛 -是的
- Family time is so important. - Uh-huh.

112
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:20,820
所以我們給爸爸們提供14個月的帶薪陪產假
That's why we offer 14 months paid paternity leave.

113
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:23,740
我們來看一下那個無限纖薄模型的最新進展
Let's see an update on that Thinfinity model.

114
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,800
設計很酷啊
Ooh. Cool design.

115
00:04:26,021 --> 00:04:28,074
-我跟誰來擊個掌 -大家
- Who do I high-five for that, huh? - Everybody.

116
00:04:28,074 --> 00:04:30,585
我們的設計會議就是走噴涌爆發風
Our design meetings are organized around burstiness,

117
00:04:30,585 --> 00:04:32,578
是一個急速創作的過程
which is a rapid-fire creative process

118
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:35,120
靠的就是解鎖潛意識的奇思妙想
that really just unlocks the unconscious.

119
00:04:36,076 --> 00:04:38,268
沒人覺得那個很分心嗎
Does anybody else find that distracting?

120
00:04:38,268 --> 00:04:40,610
事實上 那對刺激左腦有好處
Actually, it's great for left-brain stimulation.

121
00:04:40,610 --> 00:04:41,737
贏家肯定是我
I got winner!

122
00:04:42,005 --> 00:04:43,331
我們不計分
We don't keep score.

123
00:04:43,331 --> 00:04:44,488
-不計嗎 -小心
- No? - Watch out!

124
00:04:45,095 --> 00:04:45,855
什么鬼
What the hell?!

125
00:04:45,855 --> 00:04:47,895
你不知道太空球嗎
You don't know about Zorbing?

126
00:04:47,895 --> 00:04:49,449
能促進身體和大腦的平衡
It promotes mind/body balance.

127
00:04:49,449 --> 00:04:51,672
是從德國的類似項目學的
It's kind of like the German version of Flerming.

128
00:04:51,672 --> 00:04:52,808
行了 夠了
Okay, that's it.

129
00:04:52,808 --> 00:04:54,452
現在 我要教教你們
Now, I'm about to introduce you squids

130
00:04:54,452 --> 00:04:55,518
什么叫做
to a little thing called

131
00:04:55,518 --> 00:04:59,026
鞠躬盡瘁外加心力交瘁的辛勤工作
back-breaking, soul-crushing hard work.

132
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:01,940
你們這里過去五年有多少人犯過心臟病
How many heart attacks have you had here in the last five years?

133
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,680
一次都沒有嗎 我這是在哪
Zero? Where am I?!

134
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:05,920
美國人熱愛衣柜
America loves closets,

135
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,900
我是來造衣柜的 媽的
and I'm here to build them, damn it!

136
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:13,020
等我看到每早有人上班前先在車里痛哭時
And you get this back when I see people pull up in the morning

137
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:14,220
我再把乒乓球還給你們
crying in their cars.

138
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:17,540
對
Yeah.

139
00:05:21,309 --> 00:05:22,624
你非得這樣嗎
Okay, must you?

140
00:05:22,624 --> 00:05:23,750
我們一定要
You know what, we are gonna make sure

141
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:26,560
讓那個素描專家看到你最帥氣的一面
that sketch artist sees the best possible version of you.

142
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:28,055
掐掐蘋果肌 臉色會更紅潤
Let's get those apples a-shining!

143
00:05:28,055 --> 00:05:29,939
好了 住手 別掐了
Okay, okay, stop. Don't!

144
00:05:30,008 --> 00:05:32,171
你發"O"音時臉會變得很奇怪
Okay, your face gets weird when you make that "O" sound,

145
00:05:32,171 --> 00:05:33,496
別發這個音
so avoid that.

146
00:05:33,496 --> 00:05:34,713
你認真的嗎
A-Are you serious?

147
00:05:34,722 --> 00:05:36,177
被告管理的是含4個"O"音開頭的
The defendant runs the Orange County

148
00:05:36,177 --> 00:05:38,578
橘子郡海洋與鳥類組織
Oceanic and Ornithological Organization.

149
00:05:38,578 --> 00:05:39,884
-畫面太驚悚我不忍看 -什么
- That was hard to watch. - Wha--

150
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:41,720
全體起立
All rise.

151
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,440
最后整理一下
Last looks.

152
00:05:44,468 --> 00:05:45,595
坐下
Be seated.

153
00:05:45,753 --> 00:05:49,490
普里契特先生 你可以繼續詢問證人了
Mr. Pritchett, you may resume your questioning of the witness.

154
00:05:49,490 --> 00:05:50,319
好的
Okay.

155
00:05:51,065 --> 00:05:53,098
米奇爾 米奇爾 他來了
Mitchell. Mitchell. He's here.

156
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,620
用你最好看的角度對著他
Only give him your best side.

157
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,580
別讓日光燈直射你 別發"O"音
Avoid the fluorescent lights, no O's,

158
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,540
無論你做什么 都千萬別站到那個法警旁邊
and whatever you do, do not stand next to the bailiff.

159
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:00,520
他帥得令人窒息
He is breathtaking!

160
00:06:00,851 --> 00:06:01,689
真的好帥
Oh, my God.

161
00:06:01,728 --> 00:06:02,765
律師
Counselor?

162
00:06:03,362 --> 00:06:04,778
抱歉 法官大人
Uh, sorry, Your Honor. Um...

163
00:06:05,485 --> 00:06:06,840
-卡彭特小姐... -丑臉警告
- Miss Carpenter... - Bad side!

164
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:11,200
你在案發當晚
...do you recall seeing this man

165
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:12,380
有否見過這個男人
on the night in question?

166
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,578
見過 先生
Yes, sir.

167
00:06:13,616 --> 00:06:16,247
據你所知 他是不是
And is he, to your knowledge, the C.E.O...

168
00:06:16,546 --> 00:06:20,253
橘子郡海洋與鳥類組織的總裁
of the Orange County Oceanic and Ornithological Organization?

169
00:06:20,253 --> 00:06:21,638
律師 你說話很含糊
Counselor, you're mumbling.

170
00:06:21,638 --> 00:06:23,143
請你重復一遍問題
Can you repeat that, please?

171
00:06:23,253 --> 00:06:25,126
他是不是負責管理那個鳥和水的地方
Does he run the bird and water place?

172
00:06:25,156 --> 00:06:25,993
是的
He does.

173
00:06:25,993 --> 00:06:28,744
他今天是否在...
And is he here today in this, uh...

174
00:06:31,345 --> 00:06:32,949
-我剛剛問... -再過來一點
- As I was saying... - Little further.

175
00:06:32,949 --> 00:06:35,829
他今天是否
...is he here today in this,

176
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,600
在法庭內
uh -- in this courtroom?

177
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:39,880
那個就是他
That's him.

178
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:42,340
請注意 我很肯定
Let the court note that I am pretty sure

179
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:44,820
證人已經指認出了被告
that the witness has identified the defendant.

180
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,320
肘部有補丁
Elbow patches?

181
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,840
你是不是又在鐵板燒餐廳燒壞了外套
Did you burn through another blazer at Benihana's?

182
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,220
其實是特地為新工作準備的
Actually, it is for my new position

183
00:06:58,220 --> 00:07:00,760
我要去你學校教房地產課
teaching real estate at your school.

184
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:01,700
你在說什么
What are you talking about?

185
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:02,900
他們給了我一份工作
They offered me a job.

186
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:04,560
不過 聽我說
But hey, listen -- listen to me.

187
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:05,940
先不說這是我的畢生夢想
Lifelong dreams aside,

188
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,960
還要先征求你同意 我才會接受這份工作
I'm not taking this unless you're on board.

189
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,020
我絕對不同意
I'm definitely not.

190
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:11,900
我懂
I get it.

191
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:13,900
你不希望被自己老爸破壞了形象
Don't want your old Pops cramping your style,

192
00:07:14,345 --> 00:07:15,542
所以我不去了
so I'm -- I'm out.

193
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:16,380
說來好笑
It's just funny.

194
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:18,480
我都不記得上次這么興奮是幾時的事了
Can't remember the last time I was this excited.

195
00:07:18,849 --> 00:07:19,896
但除非你也為此興奮
But it wouldn't -- wouldn't make any sense

196
00:07:19,896 --> 00:07:21,191
否則這事就沒意思了
unless you were excited, too.

197
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:22,468
我的內心沒有一絲波瀾
Not even a little bit.

198
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:23,680
好吧
Right.

199
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:26,160
不過那些孩子真可憐
Those poor kids, though, huh?

200
00:07:26,582 --> 00:07:28,167
我有那么多知識可以教給他們
I have so much to offer.

201
00:07:28,446 --> 00:07:29,492
比如說
For example,

202
00:07:29,492 --> 00:07:33,100
銷售不同風格的房屋時應分別搭配哪些餅干
which house styles are sold by which cookie type?

203
00:07:33,249 --> 00:07:34,425
法國折衷主義風格
French Revival --

204
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:35,100
搭配馬卡龍
Macaroons.

205
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,180
英國都鐸風格
English Tudor --

206
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:37,460
搭配牛油酥餅
shortbread.

207
00:07:39,020 --> 00:07:41,300
但 我明白你的想法
But... we both know what you want,

208
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:44,151
所以我會辭職
so, uh, I'll resign and go back

209
00:07:44,151 --> 00:07:47,529
繼續思考我退休前的年頭可以做些什么
to trying to figure out what to do with my final years.

210
00:07:47,529 --> 00:07:48,308
好
Okay.

211
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:54,640
我需要找個地方借住幾天
I need a place to stay for a couple of days.

212
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:55,900
不能回家 也不能去學校
Can't go home, can't go to school,

213
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:56,980
我也不想談論這事
don't want to talk about it.

214
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:57,680
知道了
Got it.

215
00:07:58,260 --> 00:08:00,940
我知道艾麗克斯很想聊這事
I knew that Alex wanted to talk about it,

216
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:03,000
但我自己也有一堆煩心事
but I had a lot on my mind.

217
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:05,140
今早喬讓我很頭疼
I had a rough morning with Joe.

218
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:07,520
第一天上學愉快哦
Have a great first day.

219
00:08:08,327 --> 00:08:10,390
你不送我進去嗎
Aren't you gonna walk me in?

220
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:13,290
不送 一年級學生都定點下車自己走進去的
No. In first grade, you have drop-off.

221
00:08:13,290 --> 00:08:15,761
沒人說過有這件事啊
No one said anything about drop-off.

222
00:08:15,761 --> 00:08:17,515
要是我找不到我放東西的格子怎么辦
What if I can't find my cubby?

223
00:08:17,515 --> 00:08:19,887
學校沒有小格子 只有儲物柜
They don't have cubbies. They have lockers here.

224
00:08:19,887 --> 00:08:22,717
等一下 等一下 我的午餐盒呢
Wait. Wait a second. Where's my lunchbox?

225
00:08:22,717 --> 00:08:25,677
我幫你申請了在學校用餐
Oh, I signed you up for the hot-lunch program.

226
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:27,580
這里到底是什么鬼地方
What is this place?

227
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,920
我最近有些壓力
Okay, I've been feeling some pressure

228
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,640
不知道今年畢業后該做什么
about what to do after I graduate this year,

229
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:33,600
我爸媽又一直問個不停
and my parents are constantly asking me about it.

230
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:35,280
你不是打算工作嗎
I thought that you were going to work.

231
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:38,920
我本來也這么想 但最近我質疑一切
So did I, but lately, I've been questioning everything.

232
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:41,080
我甚至考慮要當研究生[男人]
I even thought about becoming a fellow.

233
00:08:41,661 --> 00:08:43,694
艾麗克斯 這可是巨大的改變
Ay, Alex, that's a big change.

234
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:45,880
但至少你的名字通用
But at least you get to keep the same name.

235
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:47,520
我都不確定我是否真想這么做
I'm not even sure it's what I really want.

236
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:48,920
你得考慮清楚了
Okay, you have to be very sure,

237
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:51,580
因為我聽說要變回去更難
because I heard it's even harder to reverse it.

238
00:08:51,756 --> 00:08:53,490
我們能聊點別的嗎 喬人呢
Can we talk about anything else? Where's Joe?

239
00:08:53,490 --> 00:08:55,154
他今天開始上小學
He started school today.

240
00:08:55,154 --> 00:08:57,944
我在校門口放他下車時 他很慌
He was so panicky when I dropped him off.

241
00:08:58,014 --> 00:08:59,858
我不知道為什么 不過是一年級而已嘛
I don't know why. It's just first grade.

242
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:00,860
不過是一年級而已
Just first grade?!

243
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,360
壓力就是從那時開始的
That's when the pressure starts!

244
00:09:02,488 --> 00:09:04,084
你要嚇死人家啦
Ay! You're freaking me out!

245
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:07,760
艾麗克斯以后會是一個神經質的男人
Alex is going to be a very nervous man.

246
00:09:09,952 --> 00:09:11,537
不好意思 畫素描的
Uh, e-excuse me, sketch man.

247
00:09:11,537 --> 00:09:13,640
-我們想跟你聊聊你的畫 -對
- We'd like a word with you about your little drawings. - Yes.

248
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:15,184
你們不記得我了 對吧
You don't remember me, do you?

249
00:09:16,918 --> 00:09:17,876
你是...
It's -- Um...

250
00:09:18,453 --> 00:09:21,054
很明顯我們得罪過你
Well, obviously, we have offended you somehow.

251
00:09:21,054 --> 00:09:23,126
你是我們害你被炒魷魚的咖啡師 對嗎
Oh, were you the barista we had fired?

252
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:26,120
給你們個提示 我租過你們家樓上的房間
Here's a hint -- I once stayed in your upstairs rental.

253
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:29,440
誰會用光一整籃迎賓用品啊
Who consumes an entire welcome basket?

254
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:31,120
我們通常有一半能重復使用
We usually reuse half this stuff.

255
00:09:31,180 --> 00:09:33,040
薄荷糖都吃光了 他不過住了一晚而已
All the Altoids. He was here one night.

256
00:09:33,181 --> 00:09:35,304
連辣根芥末醬都吃完了
He -- He even ate the horseradish mustard.

257
00:09:35,304 --> 00:09:36,350
他都拿來蘸什么吃了
What did he put it on?

258
00:09:36,350 --> 00:09:38,642
我們故意沒提供餅干啊
We purposely don't give crackers.

259
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:46,100
很抱歉我們如此失禮 可是
We are so sorry we offended you, but --

260
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:46,880
道歉來不及了
Ooh, too late.

261
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:48,240
你倆任我魚肉
I own you two.

262
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:50,560
我還沒用上大絕招呢
And I haven't even gotten to my best stuff yet.

263
00:09:51,140 --> 00:09:52,420
我還可以把你畫得更紅
I can go redder.

264
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:53,620
你不會的
You wouldn't.

265
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:55,320
等我把你畫成一字眉你就知道厲害了
Just wait till I connect the brows.

266
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:55,960
求你善良
Please.

267
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:57,620
我們還有個孩子
We have a child.

268
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:01,300
有意思了 CNN臺的記者
Oh, fun -- a reporter from CNN.

269
00:10:01,493 --> 00:10:04,323
看來這幅畫像就要被全國人民看到了
Looks like this pretty little portrait's about to go national.

270
00:10:05,250 --> 00:10:06,784
我們該怎么辦
Uh... What-what are we gonna do?

271
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,320
只有我這么想嗎 聽起來
Okay, is it just me, or does this sound

272
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:10,340
-該知識索引瓊斯登場了 -只有你
- like a job for Thesaurus Jones? - It's just you.

273
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:11,780
不 我指黒函威脅他 米奇爾
No. Blackmail, Mitchell!

274
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,300
我們得挖點這個人的黑料
We just have to dig something up on this guy.

275
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:16,040
應該問題不大 因為每個人
Shouldn't be a problem, because everyone's

276
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:16,740
都有想藏的秘密
hiding something.

277
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:18,480
每個人
Everyone.

278
00:10:19,759 --> 00:10:21,423
我感覺你還想再說一次
I feel like you're sitting on one more...

279
00:10:21,423 --> 00:10:22,620
-每個人 -沒錯
- Everyone. - Yep.

280
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,280
我害怕的事發生了
Just as I feared,

281
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:33,780
我爸碾壓了辦公室所有人的精氣神
my dad had crushed the spirit of everyone in that office.

282
00:10:34,060 --> 00:10:35,480
我必須想辦法證明
I had to do something to prove

283
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:37,140
我們不是古板的掃興鬼
we weren't some stuffy killjoys.

284
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:39,660
是時候放出派對克萊爾了
It was time to bust out Party Claire.

285
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:43,120
89年春假后她引退了
She'd retired after spring break '89.

286
00:10:43,686 --> 00:10:45,142
92年又引退了一次
And again in '92.

287
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:47,760
你有時間嗎
Hey, do you have a second?

288
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:50,140
如果你想說我不尊重你們的方法
If this is about my respecting your process --

289
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:52,700
其實我們想謝謝你之前立威
Actually, we want to thank you for laying down the law before.

290
00:10:52,764 --> 00:10:54,269
因為我們作為一個公司已經沒樣子了
Because we have gone soft as a company,

291
00:10:54,269 --> 00:10:55,804
我們需要幾個成熟的人加入
we needed a couple grown-ups to come in

292
00:10:55,804 --> 00:10:57,209
讓我們重回正軌
and put us back on track.

293
00:10:57,209 --> 00:10:58,116
多虧了你
You know, thanks to you,

294
00:10:58,460 --> 00:10:59,620
我們那些分散注意力的東西都撤走了
we've gotten rid of all the distractions --

295
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:01,700
乒乓球桌和水槍都撤走了
no more ping-pong tables, squirt guns.

296
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,460
我們唯一沒找到的是那個巨大的...
The only thing we couldn't find was that giant --

297
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:05,160
休息時間 賤人們
Break time, bitches!

298
00:11:07,314 --> 00:11:08,310
原來這有點...
Uh, it turns out this is a little --

299
00:11:08,310 --> 00:11:09,855
我的天 無限纖薄模型
Oh, my God! The Thinfinity!

300
00:11:09,855 --> 00:11:10,841
我很抱歉
I'm so sorry!

301
00:11:10,841 --> 00:11:12,805
我的天 太對不起了
Oh, my God! I'm so sorry!

302
00:11:12,805 --> 00:11:13,712
我...
I -- Oh!

303
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:18,120
對不起
Sorry.

304
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:27,000
畫畫那小子也保養得太好了
Sketch boy was unusually well-groomed

305
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
政府補貼的健身房不可能有這效果
for somebody coming out of a government-subsidized gym.

306
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:31,660
其中肯定有貓膩
Something wasn't right.

307
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:34,520
知識索引瓊斯的鼻子聞出來了
I was getting that old Thesaurus Jones tingle.

308
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:36,680
我決定四處嗅探一下
I decided to do some sniffing around.

309
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:40,120
那畫畫的臉上有種光彩
Sketch guy's face had a kind of glow

310
00:11:41,305 --> 00:11:44,066
只有用了昂貴的潤膚霜才會有
that can only be achieved with expensive creams and unguents,

311
00:11:44,066 --> 00:11:47,324
而我只找到了幾包廉價的通用乳液
yet all I found were packets of cut-rate all-purpose lotions.

312
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:50,040
根據我的信息源 健身房有個領導樓層
According to my sources, the gym had an executive level

313
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,420
能提供各種高級水療護膚品
that provides all manner of fancy spa products,

314
00:11:52,820 --> 00:11:54,760
但只有法官和律師才能加入
but it's for judges and attorneys only.

315
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:58,280
我聲東擊西 告訴保全人員
I created a diversion by convincing the security detail

316
00:11:58,280 --> 00:11:59,860
毛巾出了些緊急狀況
there was a towel emergency...

317
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,420
毛巾出了些緊急狀況
There's a towel emergency.

318
00:12:05,460 --> 00:12:08,220
并黑進了健身房的電腦系統
...and hacked into the gym's computer system.

319
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:11,540
原來他一直在偷偷進入領導層
Turns out he's been accessing the executive level

320
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:12,800
靠的是盜刷
by swiping the ID

321
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:15,860
一位退休法官 維克多·格雷厄姆的卡
of one Victor Graham, a retired judge.

322
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,080
各位陪審員
Members of the jury,

323
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:22,560
被告凱恩先生想讓你們認為
the defendant, Mr. Kane, would have you believe

324
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:25,240
在罪案發生時他正在工作
that he was working at the time of the crime.

325
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,240
光頭[大膽]
Bald?!

326
00:12:27,463 --> 00:12:30,933
厚顏的謊言
...faced lies!

327
00:12:31,351 --> 00:12:32,359
律師
Counselor?

328
00:12:33,404 --> 00:12:36,762
因為證據明顯表明
Because evidence would clearly suggest that, um...

329
00:12:39,373 --> 00:12:41,177
盡管詹姆斯·凱恩
...that while James Kane

330
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:45,422
的確在他公司的領導樓層有間辦公室
does have an office on his company's executive floor,

331
00:12:45,422 --> 00:12:47,495
那晚他根本就沒有去
he was nowhere near it that night.

332
00:12:47,495 --> 00:12:50,734
想得美 領導層詹姆[健身房]
Nice try, executive-level Jim.

333
00:12:51,410 --> 00:12:52,250
凱恩
...Kane,

334
00:12:53,653 --> 00:12:55,030
可我們盯上你了
but we're onto you.

335
00:12:55,338 --> 00:12:58,506
女士們先生們 在你們退庭[退休]前
Ladies and gentlemen, before you've retired,

336
00:12:58,506 --> 00:13:01,795
自己判斷[法官]
judge...for yourself

337
00:13:01,795 --> 00:13:06,499
繪制一幅更切實的結論圖
and draw a more accurate conclusion

338
00:13:06,499 --> 00:13:08,811
比凱恩先生想讓你們相信的話更切實
than the one Mr. Kane would have you believe...

339
00:13:08,811 --> 00:13:10,654
律師 你說的話很奇怪
Counselor, you're speaking weirdly.

340
00:13:11,142 --> 00:13:13,873
我肯定你們會發現被告的不在場證明
I'm sure you will find the defendant's alibi

341
00:13:13,873 --> 00:13:15,557
非常不可信[苗條]
to be thin.

342
00:13:15,950 --> 00:13:17,050
甚至更不可信[苗條]
Even thinner.

343
00:13:20,819 --> 00:13:21,846
謝謝你
Thank you.

344
00:13:23,530 --> 00:13:26,390
下午好 年輕的房地產經紀人們
Good afternoon, young realtors.

345
00:13:26,790 --> 00:13:30,350
下課后我有重要事情宣布
I have a very important announcement to make after class,

346
00:13:30,350 --> 00:13:31,890
在那之前
but in the meantime,

347
00:13:31,890 --> 00:13:34,870
請你們配合地打開書本
if you would be so kind as to open your books --

348
00:13:36,470 --> 00:13:37,910
老天 我做不到
Oh, boy. I can't do this.

349
00:13:38,410 --> 00:13:41,930
同學們 今天是我們最后一天一起上課了
Students, today is our last day together.

350
00:13:44,210 --> 00:13:46,030
我很珍視我們在一起的時間
I've treasured our time together.

351
00:13:46,890 --> 00:13:49,110
布雷特 我知道我們最開始有點矛盾
Brett, I know we got off to a rough start,

352
00:13:49,150 --> 00:13:50,730
但當我們消除那些隔閡后
but once we broke down those walls,

353
00:13:50,770 --> 00:13:52,210
我都不知道誰教了對方更多
I'm not sure who was teaching who.

354
00:13:53,953 --> 00:13:56,973
惠特尼 你是我所認識最堅強的單身母親
Whitney, you're the toughest single mother I know.

355
00:13:56,973 --> 00:13:58,697
露西 對你媽好一些
Lucy, you be good to your mom.

356
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:01,830
包包 你與閱讀障礙抗爭太了不起了
Bob, amazing how you battle that dyslexia.

357
00:14:02,763 --> 00:14:04,985
不過你或許不該再對父母那么憤怒
Maybe ease off on the anger toward your parents, though.

358
00:14:04,985 --> 00:14:06,988
他們給你起的名字給你省了很多麻煩
They did you a solid giving you that name.

359
00:14:06,988 --> 00:14:08,722
我們會想您的 爾菲老師
We're gonna miss you, Mr. Nudphy.

360
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:10,795
你又說反了 不過
It's -- You -- You -- You flipped it, but...

361
00:14:10,795 --> 00:14:12,559
我也會想你們的
I'm gonna miss you guys, too.

362
00:14:13,730 --> 00:14:15,710
地段 地段 地段
Location. Location. Location.

363
00:14:16,410 --> 00:14:18,310
你記住了
You memorized it.

364
00:14:19,190 --> 00:14:22,550
第二次也是最后一次
Now, for the second and last time...

365
00:14:23,939 --> 00:14:25,364
下課
class dismissed.

366
00:14:27,470 --> 00:14:27,990
爸
Dad.

367
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:29,230
盧克
Luke?

368
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:31,570
你在教室后面多久了
How long have you been back there?

369
00:14:31,950 --> 00:14:33,210
我基本上看到了一切
I pretty much saw the whole thing.

370
00:14:35,250 --> 00:14:36,550
-爸 -怎么
- Hey, Dad? - Yeah?

371
00:14:38,110 --> 00:14:39,510
別忘了你的咖啡杯
Don't forget your coffee mug.

372
00:14:43,310 --> 00:14:45,170
我相信這是最好的結果
I'm sure this all worked out for the best.

373
00:14:46,062 --> 00:14:47,746
我或許會想念
I'll, uh, probably miss

374
00:14:47,746 --> 00:14:50,217
一些隨性的扔飛盤的機會
a few spontaneous Frisbee opportunities and...

375
00:14:50,606 --> 00:14:52,918
顯然還有翻跟頭交換生項目
apparently, a tumbling exchange program --

376
00:14:52,918 --> 00:14:55,688
好吧 還有業余發明家協會
oh, well -- and an Amateur Inventors Association.

377
00:14:55,688 --> 00:14:58,040
反正改變世界八成也沒什么意思
How much fun could it be changing the world, anyway?

378
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:01,690
"紅杉大學選手為您呈現
"The Sequoia College Players Present:

379
00:15:01,690 --> 00:15:05,010
霍爾與奧茲魔術表演"
A Hall and Oates Magic Show."

380
00:15:07,270 --> 00:15:08,790
-爸 等等 -怎么 盧克
- Dad, wait. - Yes, Luke?

381
00:15:09,610 --> 00:15:10,710
這次也別忘了咖啡杯
Don't forget your mug again.

382
00:15:11,350 --> 00:15:12,150
拜托
Come on!

383
00:15:12,570 --> 00:15:14,290
你看不出我來這是命中注定嗎
Can't you see I'm meant to be here?

384
00:15:14,430 --> 00:15:16,950
抱歉 只是我從來沒獨自上過學
I'm sorry, but I've never had a school to myself.

385
00:15:17,652 --> 00:15:19,406
過去我總是艾麗克斯的傻弟弟
I was always Alex's dumb brother

386
00:15:19,406 --> 00:15:21,190
或曼尼的性感侄子
or Manny's hot nephew.

387
00:15:21,379 --> 00:15:23,462
現在我終于能做自己了
Now I can finally be my own person.

388
00:15:23,711 --> 00:15:25,127
抱歉 我理解
I'm sorry. I get it.

389
00:15:25,505 --> 00:15:27,348
我真的理解
I-I r-I-I really do.

390
00:15:27,388 --> 00:15:29,242
我想我只是興奮過頭了
I think I was just getting a little overexcited.

391
00:15:29,242 --> 00:15:29,940
我
I'll, uh...

392
00:15:31,070 --> 00:15:32,290
我們家里見
I'll see you at home.

393
00:15:34,573 --> 00:15:35,350
鄧菲
Dunphy.

394
00:15:35,350 --> 00:15:38,360
真高興撞見你了 我想當面恭喜你
Glad I ran into you so I can congratulate you personally.

395
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:39,476
等等 我入選球隊了嗎
Wait. I made the team?

396
00:15:39,476 --> 00:15:40,493
先發球員
First string.

397
00:15:40,502 --> 00:15:44,299
不得不說 你舉人爭球的姿勢一看就是練家子
I got to say, your form on that lineout lift was impeccable.

398
00:15:44,329 --> 00:15:45,516
-謝謝 -是啊
- Thanks. - Yeah.

399
00:15:51,070 --> 00:15:52,910
爸 我入選球隊了
Hey, Dad. I made the team.

400
00:15:53,270 --> 00:15:54,030
太棒了
That's amazing!

401
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:56,010
我就知道你會入選 你是天生好手
I knew you would. You're a natural.

402
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:57,650
我有個很好的老師
Well, I had a great teacher.

403
00:15:59,810 --> 00:16:00,570
你聽我說
So, listen.

404
00:16:00,810 --> 00:16:02,550
校區挺大的
This is a big campus.

405
00:16:03,330 --> 00:16:04,830
或許我們可以在此共存
Maybe we could both be here

406
00:16:04,830 --> 00:16:07,030
只要我們保證不在對方面前晃悠
if we promise to stay out of each other's way.

407
00:16:09,050 --> 00:16:10,870
我很不想踩進你的地盤的
Well, I'd hate to step on your toes.

408
00:16:11,146 --> 00:16:12,591
不會 你不會
No, no, y-you wouldn't.

409
00:16:12,750 --> 00:16:13,950
我也不想阻止你
I would hate to stop you

410
00:16:13,950 --> 00:16:15,190
去做一些你很擅長的事情
from doing something you're so good at.

411
00:16:15,410 --> 00:16:16,890
我可以考慮考慮
I guess I could think about it.

412
00:16:16,970 --> 00:16:19,650
其實我也不是整天都泡在這里
I mean, it's not like I'd be there all the time.

413
00:16:19,935 --> 00:16:22,984
畢竟我得上課 還得上班
I, uh, have class and office hours,

414
00:16:22,984 --> 00:16:25,755
我每周二四的早上11點到下午2點
and I have the 11:00 A.M. to 2:00 P.M. slot

415
00:16:25,755 --> 00:16:29,452
也得負責搞校園電臺的事情
at the campus radio station on Tuesdays and Thursdays.

416
00:16:29,452 --> 00:16:31,654
如果你想當我的助手...
Hey, if you want to be my sidekick...

417
00:16:32,290 --> 00:16:33,810
-老爸 -你說得對
- Dad? - You're right.

418
00:16:33,830 --> 00:16:34,930
最好還是我獨自為節目發聲吧
It's better if I do all the voices.

419
00:16:35,430 --> 00:16:35,950
怎么著
What's up?!

420
00:16:39,050 --> 00:16:39,870
這些是什么
What's all this?

421
00:16:40,310 --> 00:16:43,450
你讓我好緊張喬今天會不開心
Well, you got me so nervous about Joe's terrible day

422
00:16:43,450 --> 00:16:45,930
我就先把這些擺出來好哄他開心
that I put all this out to cheer him up --

423
00:16:45,974 --> 00:16:48,117
圣代 電子游戲
sundae, video game.

424
00:16:48,117 --> 00:16:50,519
我還給他寫了段鼓舞的話
I even wrote him a little pep talk.

425
00:16:50,590 --> 00:16:52,210
我們能活在藥品的黃金時期真是太好了
We're lucky to live in the golden age of medicines.

426
00:16:52,550 --> 00:16:54,310
外公 我要在這里住幾天
Hey, Grandpa, I'm staying here for a couple of days,

427
00:16:54,310 --> 00:16:55,530
我也不想聊到底為什么
and I do not want to talk about it.

428
00:16:55,570 --> 00:16:55,910
行
Cool.

429
00:16:57,270 --> 00:16:58,070
喬回來了
That's Joe.

430
00:17:02,150 --> 00:17:03,910
我老爸在家嗎
Hey, is my dad home?

431
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:05,650
靠 我媽來這里干嘛
Crap. What is my mom doing here?

432
00:17:05,650 --> 00:17:06,150
跟我來
Come with me.

433
00:17:07,061 --> 00:17:08,695
我欠他一句抱歉
I owe him an apology.

434
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:10,470
我在公司給他出了大丑
I made a huge scene at work.

435
00:17:11,290 --> 00:17:14,530
有時候跟人道歉的最好方法
Well, sometimes the best way to say "I'm sorry"

436
00:17:14,555 --> 00:17:15,571
就是通過電郵
is in an e-mail.

437
00:17:15,571 --> 00:17:20,434
你何不寫封道歉函到"杰的電腦郵件@aol.com"呢
Why don't you write him at JaysComputerMail@aol.com?

438
00:17:20,950 --> 00:17:23,950
我用一個巨型倉鼠球碾了一群人
I plowed over a bunch of people in a giant hamster ball.

439
00:17:23,950 --> 00:17:25,550
然后我試著討好公司里的美食粉
And then I tried to impress the foodies

440
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:27,090
所以點了印度菜當午餐
by ordering Indian for lunch.

441
00:17:27,291 --> 00:17:28,427
而為了去掉我口中的
And then I chewed some gum

442
00:17:28,427 --> 00:17:29,971
香菜味 我嚼了口香糖
to get rid of my coriander breath,

443
00:17:29,971 --> 00:17:31,835
我挺確定現在粘到我頭發上了
and I'm pretty sure some's in my hair.

444
00:17:31,835 --> 00:17:33,399
接著我...
And then I -- Oh --

445
00:17:33,790 --> 00:17:35,850
被絆倒然后把膝蓋跌破皮了
tripped and fell and skinned my knee,

446
00:17:35,850 --> 00:17:37,970
而且還讓大家看到了我的內褲
and everybody saw my underwear.

447
00:17:38,930 --> 00:17:39,550
牛逼爆了
Crushed it!

448
00:17:39,830 --> 00:17:41,550
只要人酷 第一天上學簡直太簡單了
First days are easy when you're cool.

449
00:17:42,677 --> 00:17:44,411
但我有點可憐康納·B同學
I do feel bad for Conner B.

450
00:17:44,610 --> 00:17:47,570
他帶的雞蛋沙拉午餐都臭了
He brought stinky egg salad for lunch.

451
00:17:48,110 --> 00:17:49,990
他以后只能去找護士阿姨吃飯了
He's gonna have to eat with the nurse.

452
00:17:50,310 --> 00:17:51,596
天啊
Oh, God! Ay.

453
00:17:52,074 --> 00:17:54,247
喬 你先上樓待著吧
Uh, Joe, why don't you go upstairs?

454
00:17:54,970 --> 00:17:56,990
我只想回到我以前的公司
I just want to go back to my old office,

455
00:17:56,990 --> 00:17:57,970
我在那里有朋友
where I had friends.

456
00:17:58,510 --> 00:17:59,590
我理解
I know.

457
00:18:00,150 --> 00:18:00,790
有時候...
Sometimes...

458
00:18:00,810 --> 00:18:03,990
我們都有不順的日子
...you know, we all have bad days.

459
00:18:05,810 --> 00:18:06,450
而...
And...

460
00:18:06,843 --> 00:18:11,477
而有時候我們得... 面對壞男生
And sometimes, we have to -- to deal with mean boys.

461
00:18:11,477 --> 00:18:12,742
臭男生最壞了
Boys are mean.

462
00:18:13,790 --> 00:18:14,370
你說得對 歌洛莉亞
You're right, Gloria.

463
00:18:15,010 --> 00:18:15,830
我說得對啊
I am right?

464
00:18:17,190 --> 00:18:19,950
你知道我最愛這個家庭什么嗎
Oh, you know what I love about this family?

465
00:18:20,590 --> 00:18:23,610
我們永不退縮 尤其是你
We're not quitters -- especially you.

466
00:18:24,810 --> 00:18:28,330
還記得你當時學游泳碰到了多少困難嗎
Remember how hard it was for you to learn how to swim?

467
00:18:29,010 --> 00:18:30,030
的確很難
It was hard.

468
00:18:31,270 --> 00:18:34,270
但現在它是你最愛的一項事物
But now it's your favorite thing in the world

469
00:18:34,270 --> 00:18:37,790
因為它能讓你意識到自己多強大
because it reminds you of how strong you are.

470
00:18:37,895 --> 00:18:39,459
我的確是喜歡游泳啦 但...
I mean, I like to swim...

471
00:18:39,509 --> 00:18:41,662
觸底就會反彈 明天只會更好
Tomorrow can only be better.

472
00:18:42,390 --> 00:18:44,870
但為了以防萬一 我午餐時間會來
But just in case, I'll come at lunch,

473
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:47,290
我會隔著圍欄親親你的小臉
and I will kiss you through the fence.

474
00:18:48,328 --> 00:18:49,863
我大概11點給你發消息
How about I text you around 11:00

475
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:51,270
告訴你我的情況好不好如何
and let you know how I'm doing?

476
00:18:51,826 --> 00:18:54,058
你想告訴我為什么要躲著你媽媽嗎
So, you want to tell me why you're avoiding your mom?

477
00:18:54,058 --> 00:18:55,194
我沒有在躲她
I'm not avoiding her.

478
00:18:55,194 --> 00:18:56,739
這... 這些是什么啊
Hey, what's -- what's all this?

479
00:18:56,739 --> 00:18:59,649
危險奧沙哥的紀念品 我是個瘋狂收藏家
Danger O'Shea memorabilia. I'm a big collector.

480
00:18:59,649 --> 00:19:00,825
誰是危險奧沙哥啊
Who's Danger O'Shea?

481
00:19:01,470 --> 00:19:02,390
傳說中的大膽王
Legendary daredevil.

482
00:19:02,390 --> 00:19:04,970
以騎著摩托車飛越學校大巴而出名
Got famous for jumping over a school bus on his motorcycle.

483
00:19:05,230 --> 00:19:06,730
過來 跟我談談
Get over here! Talk to me.

484
00:19:06,790 --> 00:19:08,030
告訴我你為什么在躲你媽
Tell me why you're avoiding your mom.

485
00:19:08,970 --> 00:19:09,170
好吧
Okay.

486
00:19:09,210 --> 00:19:12,350
我這一輩子都在走科研的道路
Well, I've been on a science track my whole life,

487
00:19:12,350 --> 00:19:14,990
我父母也很喜歡 咱家的"科學家艾麗克斯"
which my parents love -- "Alex the scientist."

488
00:19:15,170 --> 00:19:17,670
但最近... 我心里有些別的的想法
But...lately, I've been having second thoughts.

489
00:19:17,915 --> 00:19:20,197
我一直很愛唱歌 而最近我也去了
I've always loved singing, and -- and I've been doing

490
00:19:20,197 --> 00:19:22,210
開麥之夜嘗試了表演
some open-mic nights recently,

491
00:19:22,210 --> 00:19:23,615
反饋還真的挺不錯的
and it's been going really well.

492
00:19:23,615 --> 00:19:26,127
我明白你想說的了 唱給我聽
I see where this is going. Sing for me.

493
00:19:26,196 --> 00:19:27,950
什么 現在嗎
What, like...right now?

494
00:19:27,950 --> 00:19:28,918
你就唱吧
Just sing.

495
00:19:31,767 --> 00:19:31,768
? 在彩虹之上的某處 ?
♪ Somewhere over the rainbow ♪

496
00:19:34,390 --> 00:19:35,450
Over the rainbow

497
00:19:36,830 --> 00:19:39,570
? 天空很藍 ?
♪ Skies are blue ♪

498
00:19:40,330 --> 00:19:41,670
很棒呢
That was great.

499
00:19:42,870 --> 00:19:43,930
好好做科研
Stick to science.

500
00:19:44,283 --> 00:19:46,904
你家的人可真是懂怎么鼓勵人呢
Wow. You really got a knack for pep talks in this house.

501
00:19:46,904 --> 00:19:48,887
我不是說你肯定不行
I'm not saying it's impossible.

502
00:19:48,887 --> 00:19:50,611
我只是讓你賭贏面大的
I'm saying play the odds.

503
00:19:50,611 --> 00:19:52,455
舉例來說 比如那個奧沙哥
For example, you take this O'Shea guy.

504
00:19:52,455 --> 00:19:53,452
棒棒噠 又回到了他上面
Oh, good. We're back to him.

505
00:19:53,452 --> 00:19:54,518
他不要命但是聰明
But he was smart.

506
00:19:54,518 --> 00:19:57,328
他創立了一家公司 站穩了腳步
He started a business, got established.

507
00:19:57,328 --> 00:19:59,082
當他發現自己還是想去追搏命的夢想
And when he couldn't kick the daredevil dream,

508
00:19:59,082 --> 00:20:00,098
他就去了
he went for it.

509
00:20:00,098 --> 00:20:02,101
他真的很厲害 超強
And he was good -- real good --

510
00:20:02,101 --> 00:20:03,756
直到滑鐵盧的那天 他試著
until that fateful day he tried to jump

511
00:20:03,756 --> 00:20:06,775
開學校大巴飛越過摩托車
over a motorcycle in a school bus.

512
00:20:06,895 --> 00:20:08,888
幸好 雖然特技沒成功
Fortunately for him, unlike his act,

513
00:20:08,888 --> 00:20:10,223
可是他有個安全保障
he had a safety net.

514
00:20:10,223 --> 00:20:11,937
-他的生意 -立刻回到商場上
- His business. - Jumped right back in.

515
00:20:11,937 --> 00:20:13,412
不到一年 生意超越了頂峰
Within a year, it was bigger than ever.

516
00:20:14,110 --> 00:20:17,070
我想說的是 你已經走這條科研道路15年了
The point is, you've been on the science track for 15 years.

517
00:20:17,210 --> 00:20:19,430
走完它嘛 為自己打好基礎
See it through. Build a foundation.

518
00:20:19,650 --> 00:20:21,970
如果過幾年你還忍不住想唱
If in a couple of years, you still have the singing bug,

519
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:22,990
大膽去啊
go for it!

520
00:20:23,029 --> 00:20:24,115
我想你說得對
I guess you're right.

521
00:20:24,115 --> 00:20:25,580
